  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "mysql: Correct query attribute handling",
  "description": "This fixes dissection of queries with new clients with query attribute\nsupport to servers that don't support this.\n\n[mysql_query_attrs.pcap](/uploads/5d45e0ecbb1d26095b956c3bb388439a/mysql_query_attrs.pcap)\n\nThis file has:\n- MySQL 8.0.30 on port 8030 (supporting query attributes)\n- TiDB on port 4000 (not supporting query attributes)\n- MySQL Client 8.0.30 as client in both cases.\n\nThis was introduced in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/7422\n\nThis might need to get backported:\n```\n$ git tag --contains a89696dc2d5d2dfff3dfa3177dfe436c2d7593b9\nv3.7.2\nv3.7.3rc0\n```\n\nWith this PR:\n```\n$ ./run/tshark -r /tmp/mysql_query_attrs.pcap -d tcp.port==8030,mysql -d tcp.port==4000,mysql -Y 'mysql.caps.query_attrs || mysql.query' -Tfields -e frame.number -e mysql.version  -e mysql.caps.query_attrs -e mysql.query_attrs -e mysql.query -Eheader=y| column -t -s='    '\nframe.number  mysql.version                            mysql.caps.query_attrs  mysql.query_attrs  mysql.query\n4             8.0.30                                   1                                          \n6                                                      1                                          \n11                                                                             1                  select @@version_comment limit 1\n14                                                                             1                  SELECT 1\n24            5.7.25-TiDB-v6.2.0-alpha-681-gce41ce062  0                                          \n26                                                     1                                          \n29                                                                                                select @@version_comment limit 1\n32                                                                                                SELECT 1\n```\n\nHere you can see that on the first session both client and server set the flag and query attributes are in use.\nThe second session (frame 24-32) have the server not setting the flag, but the client does and query attributes are not in use.",
